  "description": "The proposal relates to 115 George Lane, South Woodford, E18 1AN and seeks planning permission for the change of use of the existing ground floor commercial premises to a Sui Generis hot food takeaway. The development will allow the premises to be used for the preparation and sale of hot food for takeaway and delivery purposes.\n\nThe proposal does not involve any extension to the building, increase in floorspace, or alterations to the overall building footprint. Works will primarily consist of internal reconfiguration to accommodate food service counters, storage, and staff welfare facilities necessary for the operation of the takeaway.\n\nThe system will be designed and installed in accordance with relevant environmental health guidance to minimise noise and odour impacts on neighbouring properties.\n\nThe premises is located within an established commercial high street where a variety of retail, service, and food-related uses operate. Deliveries and collections will be managed responsibly to minimise disruption, and waste will be stored within the premises and collected by licensed waste contractors in accordance with local authority requirements.\n\nOverall, the proposal represents the reuse of an existing commercial unit without increasing the scale of development and will support the vitality and viability of the George Lane town centre.",
